# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PRIVATE EXCLUSION LIST. Never committed. Its SHA-256 and the product
# codes derived from it are committed (governance/exclusion-receipt.md,
# data/reference/excluded_product_codes.csv); the tokens themselves are not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
governance/exclusion-list.local.txt
governance/exclusion_audit*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE DATA FREEZE, AND WHY PART OF IT IS NOT COMMITTED
#
# The record-level openFDA responses carry narratives, patient arrays and
# addresses, and run to hundreds of megabytes across the cohort. git is the
# wrong container for them, and PRINCIPLES rule 1's "commit the raw response"
# is departed from here deliberately, as cascadia-matter-ledger does for its
# 314 MB zip. The freeze is asserted by HASH: data/raw/manifest.json is
# committed with a SHA-256 per staged file, and src/validate.py recomputes
# every one on every run and exits non-zero if any moved.
#
# These paths are deliberately NOT in governance/freeze.toml's protected list.
# A gitignored path there FAILS OPEN (see that file).
#
# The count series (data/raw/counts/) and the classification bulk are small
# and are committed outright.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/staging/
data/raw/bulk/*.zip
data/raw/bulk/*.json
data/raw/bulk/*.part

# Derived databases are rebuilt from the freeze; not committed.
data/conformed/*.duckdb

# Build-time toolchain for the Felix class strings (Tailwind v4 CLI). The
# compiled docs/assets/felix.css is committed; the toolchain is not.
node_modules/

# Full-page renders are 6 MB each at device scale 2 and are re-made by src/render_charts.py;
# the per-chart renders and the ladder record are committed, the page renders are not.
docs/renders/page-*.png
